# Tagged PDF, PDF/A, PDF/UA, e-invoices, signatures

From the README of stationery <%= version %>. Online: <%= docs("conformance") %>.

What a standard asks for is checked with a validator, not reasoned about. veraPDF validates
PDF/A and PDF/UA. Installed (`brew install verapdf`, or the installer from verapdf.org):

```sh
verapdf --format text -v --flavour 3b invoice.pdf     # PDF/A-3b ("2b" for PDF/A-2b)
verapdf --format text -v --flavour ua1 report.pdf     # PDF/UA-1
```

Or through Docker, with nothing installed:

```sh
docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/data:ro" verapdf/cli --format text -v --flavour 3b /data/invoice.pdf
```

The line to read is `PASS` or `FAIL` for the file, and for a failure the rule's clause (6.2.11.8, 7.18.5, …).

A spec can hold the claim (`have_conformance(:pdf_a3b)`), not its validity.

